@startuml
title Line-restriction trick — two evaluation claims collapse into one
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  ParticipantBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
  LifeLineBorderColor #7A5BB5
  NoteBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  NoteBorderColor #7A5BB5
}

participant "Prover P" as P
participant "Verifier V" as V

note over V #F3EEFB
  after sum-check at layer i, V holds
  V~_{i+1}(u) = a and V~_{i+1}(u') = a'
end note

V -> V : define the line l(t) with l(0) = u and l(1) = u'
P -> V : q(t) = V~_{i+1}(l(t)), degree m, sent as m+1 coefficients
note right of V : check q(0) = a\ncheck q(1) = a'
V -> P : random t* in F
note over V #F3EEFB
  single surviving claim
  V~_{i+1}(l(t*)) = q(t*)
end note
@enduml
